# Step 86: decouple shared HEVC models from the legacy POC parser

This step begins consumer migration without removing any parser.

The one-time executor extracts `BitReader`, `SPS`, and `PPS` from `hevc_poc.py` into the neutral module `hevc_models.py`. It rewrites direct consumers to import these shared primitives from the neutral module and leaves compatibility re-exports in `hevc_poc.py`.

The executor is deliberately conservative:

- it reads the actual repository source through Python AST
- it aborts if any class is absent
- it aborts if a moved class depends on an unhandled local symbol
- it refuses unsupported multiline imports
- it compiles every generated or modified Python file before completing
- it verifies that no consumer still imports the moved symbols from `hevc_poc`

This does not migrate `parse_sps`, `parse_pps`, `parse_first_slice`, `derive_poc`, or `analyze_poc`. Those remain later consumer-migration steps.
